{"reviews":[{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-0","r":1.0,"t":"Waste of money and time","x":"I bought this for grooming clients who wanted something Extra. The first picture is one coat of polish and a second coat on the second picture and the third picture is her nails ten mins after applying the polish. The description is false. The color only pops in the bottle, it's not thick and doesn't cover the nail in only one coat. And it takes forever to dry, not a good thing when working with dogs","h":28,"v":1,"d":"Jun 2020"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-1","r":1.0,"t":"Not up to standard","x":"I bought Warren London pens before and loved them This polish has an odor. Supposed to be 6 and only 5 arrived and cant return Ugh might as well just have bought dollar store nail polish","h":11,"v":1,"d":"May 2020"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-2","r":1.0,"t":"Waste of money","x":"Just got around to using this today so missed the return window. \ud83d\ude21. What a waste of money! No matter how much shaking, it doesn't thicken. It's a very pale pink and very watery and does not dry fast. Each nail would need 12 coats just to look the color of the bottle color. Total waste of time and money.","h":5,"v":1,"d":"Feb 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-3","r":1.0,"t":"THIN, RUNNY - After 3 coats I can\u2019t tell it\u2019s been painted!","x":"My puppy\u2019s nails are clear/white with a black vein in the center.  This nail has 3 coats of this polish, and you can barely tell it\u2019s been painted.  It\u2019s so runny keeping it off her fur is next to impossible.  DO NOT BUY THIS NON-RETURNABLE PRODUCT.","h":5,"v":1,"d":"Apr 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-4","r":3.0,"t":"Needs to be thicker","x":"Dogs nails are already very difficult to do and when you have to do multiple coats, it gets even more frustrating. It would be easier if the nail polish was thicker so there was only need for one coat.","h":5,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2020"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-5","r":1.0,"t":"Would not recommend","x":"Super watery took 3 layers on my dogs white nails. Looks better on her black nails.  Would not recommend if your wanting solid colors.","h":4,"v":1,"d":"Sep 2020"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-6","r":5.0,"t":"Nails","x":"This works exactly the way it says it does! One coat provides full coverage and dries quick!","h":3,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2022"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-7","r":3.0,"t":"Disappointed","x":"The color is bright and shiny, apply as one would apply regular nail polish. My dog was adverse to the strong smell of the polish. Our dog is large (70 pounds) and though well-behaved we were unable to get her to cooperate and hold still long enough to apply and dry. Our giant Schnoodle has long hair on her feet, we used tape to hold it back out of the way, my husband held her while I quickly painted her nails. The polish needs two coats for best results and takes considerably longer than 45 sec","h":2,"v":1,"d":"May 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-8","r":4.0,"t":"Need Multiple Coats","x":"Smells awful. Odor hangs around after fully dry. Takes same amount of dry time as normal human nail polish. Needs multiple coats for decent color payoff especially with darker nails. Really pretty pinky purple though.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Feb 2022"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-9","r":1.0,"t":"No color deposit","x":"Watered down, human grade nail polish. Could work with 4 or 5 coats but good luck getting your dog to hold still for that long.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Jan 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-10","r":2.0,"t":"Meh decent","x":"Most of the colors you have to put several coats!","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Apr 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-11","r":5.0,"t":"A decent nail polish","x":"So I had to do about three coats of this nail polish on my dog's nails maybe because she has some black spots in her nails but she looks so nice it was a little hard to apply to get her to stand still after all she is probably the only South American pitbull female that is about 110 lb with pink nail polish got to love it","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Dec 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-12","r":5.0,"t":"Recommend for lighter nails","x":"Very thin, not buildable. Fast drying. Suggest not using on darker nails . My golden has darker nails and you can see it after two coats but would look much better on lighter nails.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-13","r":1.0,"t":"This is not dog nail polish!!!","x":"This is human nail polish with a dog label on it. It's probably not safe to use on any of your fur babies. My english bulldogs barks and runs away from it!! Very disappointed!!","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Jan 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-14","r":1.0,"t":"This does not smell dog safe","x":"Smells and goes on like regular nail polish. Having a hard time believing this is dog safe. Thought I\u2019d be able to return it but it\u2019s ineligible. I do not recommend.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"May 2023"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-15","r":1.0,"t":"Smells so strong and is very thin","x":"The smell of the polish was so strong my do freaked the second she got near it. I managed to get one coat on her nails and the color isn't even visible.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2023"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-16","r":4.0,"t":"Love warren london","x":"I love warren London dog nail polish and nail polish pens but this one has a very strong smell that my dog doesn\u2019t like.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Sep 2022"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-17","r":1.0,"t":"VERY STRONG SMELL","x":"The smell is so strong my dog can\u2019t stand it.. Cannot return it once it is purchased. Very disappointed","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Jan 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-18","r":5.0,"t":"Fabulous product","x":"Drys quick, covers well and dogs do not seem bothered by it. No licking or chewing after application.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2022"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-19","r":1.0,"t":"Don\u2019t waste your money.","x":"It doesn\u2019t show up on my doggies nails, plus it takes forever to dry!","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Feb 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-20","r":1.0,"t":"Disappointed","x":"Does not work well needs like 5 to 7 coats just to see","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Feb 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-21","r":1.0,"t":"Horrible!","x":"If you can manage to get past the smell, you\u2019ll hit numerous other issues. I tried this on myself first. 2 coats and 40 minutes later, wiped right off with a dry paper towel. No way I would use this on my doggo!! She\u2019d have it licked off before I got half a foot done! And no way I trust these ingredients around a dog!","h":0,"v":1,"d":"Jun 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-22","r":1.0,"t":"Not For Pets","x":"I opened up the bottle after receiving it and holy cow. I don't think I've ever smelled a nail polish so strong. There is no way that this is ok for pets. I think it gave my beautiful girl a headache. This is not worth the price or the product. $2 drug store nail polish is better than this stuff.","h":0,"v":1,"d":"May 2021"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-23","r":5.0,"t":"Easy to use","x":"This goes on mutch easier than the pen. It takes two coats with solid black nails. Polish is very bold and last the weekend. I did not like the remover for this poduct it has a strong smell just like human products and made my dog have a sneezing fit. It removes easily with a soft Emory board.","h":0,"v":1,"d":"Sep 2022"},{"id":"B08NHTHD2G-24","r":4.0,"t":"Smells like real nail polish","x":"I think this was really cute, but the only thing is that it smelled like real nail polish so my dog kept sneezing and wouldn't let me out it on her but I managed to get one nail done and it was super pretty! I think it is a little pricy though. It also is to watery to put on human hands!\ud83d\udc85","h":0,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2023"}],"emb":"","summary":{"claims":[{"text":"The polish is thin and watery, requiring multiple coats for any visible color payoff.","cites":[1,3,4,5,6,9,10,11,12,13]},{"text":"The strong smell is unpleasant and some reviewers doubt it is dog-safe.","cites":[2,8,9,14,15]},{"text":"The product is non-returnable, which frustrated buyers who were dissatisfied.","cites":[2,3,4,15]},{"text":"Some reviewers report it works well with one coat and dries quickly.","cites":[7,13]},{"text":"It performs better on lighter nails than on darker nails.","cites":[6,12,13]}]},"qa":[]}